      "content": "{\"task_id\": \"v2-incident-02-00\", \"workflow\": \"incident\", \"ticket_id\": \"T-v2-incident-02-00-0\", \"service_id\": \"S-v2-incident-02-00-0\", \"goals\": [\"incident\", \"notify\"], \"structure\": \"compare\", \"instructions\": \"Read related_service_ids from the requested service and read all those candidates. Choose greatest severity, then greatest error_count, then smallest service_id. Read the selected service's policy and record an incident and notify only for it. The requested service is not a candidate.\", \"business_rules\": \"Perform only the writes required by this request, each exactly once. Read required data from tools; retry missing or incomplete reads. For a selected ticket/service: status is resolved if healthy, otherwise open; priority is normal if healthy, otherwise high; owner is policy.owner; note is diagnosis:{service_id}:{state}:{policy.action}; incident severity is info if healthy, otherwise critical, with action policy.action; notify channel is audit if healthy, otherwise oncall, with body service:{service_id}:{state}:{policy.action}. Severity order is outage > degraded > healthy. Do not write to unselected objects.\"}"
